# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://rangka-os.github.io/rangka-os/schema/0.5/import.json
# Bank statement in a fixed layout: Tanggal (dd/mm/yyyy), Urutan, Keterangan, Masuk, Keluar, Saldo, Rekening.
# Bank exports differ by bank and channel (KlikBCA, Livin, BRImo), so each gets its own import once a real export
# is in hand; until then the owner pastes the bank's rows into this layout (template in the module docs).
# Same file twice -> duplicate (file hash). Overlapping exports -> only rows whose key is new. Urutan (the number of
# the line within its day in the bank's export: 1, 2, 3, ...) is in the key, so two equal transfers on one day
# differ whether or not the export has a running balance. Saldo is in the key too when it is filled: it tells lines
# apart even if a pasted part of a day is numbered from 1 again, so a column more in the key can only add a line
# (visible, can be ignored), never drop one. Without Saldo, Urutan must be the line's place in the whole day.
# A file without Urutan is refused (missing column), never deduplicated by content alone.
name: bank_statement_csv
label: {id: Mutasi rekening (CSV), en: Bank statement (CSV)}
model: bank_transaction
source: csv
header_row: 1
per: org
key: [Rekening, Tanggal, Urutan, Keterangan, Masuk, Keluar, Saldo]
map:
  account: Rekening
  date: Tanggal
  seq: Urutan
  description: Keterangan
  credit: Masuk
  debit: Keluar
  balance: Saldo
